# Build context for BOTH images (backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile).
# Everything listed here would otherwise be sent to the Docker daemon on every
# `docker compose build`, and some of it must never reach an image at all.

# ---- Secrets: never bake these into an image ------------------------------
**/.env

# ---- Heavy artifacts that the images build or fetch themselves ------------
#   backend/.venv   ~113 MB  - the Dockerfile installs requirements.txt
#   frontend/node_modules ~279 MB - the Dockerfile runs `yarn install`
#   frontend/build           - the Dockerfile runs `yarn build`
#   backend/models/*.onnx    ~327 MB - fetched at container start into a volume
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/build
**/models
**/*.onnx
**/.yarn

# ---- Regenerable caches ---------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.cache
**/coverage
**/yarn-error.log
logs
**/logs

# ---- VCS / editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------
.git
**/.git
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Local-only files -----------------------------------------------------
# (design_guidelines.json IS shipped: /api/source/download zips it.)
*.zip
